      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner Unicolors, the owner of copyrights in various fabric designs, fled a copyright infringement action against H&M Hennes & Mauritz (H&M)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "certiorari to the united states court of appeals for the ninth circuit No. 20\u2013915. Argued November 8, 2021\u2014Decided February 24, 2022"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Melissa N. Patterson",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Melissa N. Patterson argued the cause for the United States as amicus curiae supporting petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "H&M",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "H&M argued that Unicolors' registration certifcate was inaccurate because Unicolors had improperly fled a single application seeking registration for 31 separate works."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0000-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In our view, however, \u00a7 411(b) does not distinguish between a mistake of law and a mistake of fact. Lack of knowledge of either fact or law can excuse an inaccuracy in a copyright registration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "H&M",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "H&M also argues that our interpretation is foreclosed by the legal maxim that \u201cignorance of the law is no excuse.\u201d See Brief for Respondent 41\u201343. This maxim \u201cnormally applies where a defendant has the requisite mental state in respect to the elements of [a] crime but claims to be unaware of the existence of a statute proscribing his conduct.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "H&M",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Finally, H&M claims that neither Unicolors' petition for certiorari nor the Ninth Circuit's opinion addressed the question we decide here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0001-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A copyright registration is invalid if the registrant included materially inaccurate information in its application \u201cwith knowledge that [the information] was inaccurate.\u201d 17 U. S. C. \u00a7 411(b)(1)(A). In its petition for certiorari, Unicolors asked us to decide a question on which the Courts of Appeals were split: whether \u00a7 411(b)(1)(A)'s \u201cknowledge\u201d element requires \u201cindicia of fraud.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0001-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit therefore explicitly addressed the question we here decide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Unicolors",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Agreeing with the Eleventh Circuit, Unicolors argued in its petition for certiorari that \u201cknowledge\u201d requires \u201cinten[t] to defraud.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States, as amicus supporting Unicolors, agrees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0001-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court misapplies Rule 14.1(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fbba9e12b6e0b0b17302a0fb433b8dd6440b445f459a8966a4be2f2d716dce13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fbba9e12b6e0-0001-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court does not decide the question that has split the Courts of Appeals, but instead decides a question that no court has addressed."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
